    Remove hppc from the elasticsearch-impl module (#8226)
    
    The High Performance Primitive Collections library was added when this
    module still embedded the Elasticsearch 7 client, which used it.
    OpenSearch no longer depends on it and none of the other embedded
    libraries reference it either. Lucene ships its own internal copy of the
    collections it needs.
    
    Dropping it shrinks the bundle by about 1 MB. Its bundle imports and
    exports stay the same.
    
    Note that the exclusion of com.carrotsearch.randomizedtesting from the
    imported packages is still needed even though it belongs to the same
    project. OpenSearch probes for it via Class.forName() to detect its test
    framework, which bnd turns into a package import.
    
    This is part of #8214.
    
